  "reasoning_log_text": "VIP cells showed suppression by familiar stimuli and ramping activity during inter-stimulus intervals (familiar vs novel). Omission trials revealed strong VIP ramping, which was not observed in excitatory cells. Reduced activity occurred with familiar images (lowering response magnitude/sparseness) while novel stimuli drove strong responses. This supports a context-dependent switch in VIP function, linking to predictive coding concepts like anticipation and salient event detection. The study focused on L2/3 cells in mouse visual cortex."
